# Cloudflare Pages redirects. https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#
# SPA routing needs no rule here: with no top-level 404.html, Pages serves
# index.html for any path that isn't a static file, and React Router renders
# the route (or its own 404 page). A "/* /index.html 200" rule would also
# answer for missing /assets/* chunks with HTML, which breaks clients
# running an old build after a deploy.
#
# www → apex is a domain-level redirect, which _redirects can't express;
# set it up as a Cloudflare Redirect Rule (see DEPLOY.md).

# Legacy / convenience paths
/login        /auth/login         301
/signup       /auth/signup        301
/register     /auth/signup        301
/join         /auth/signup        301
